#X text 275 106 Sets how long the interval is between switching samples.;
#X text -192 223 This function sets the crossfader frequency so that it matches the sample interval., f 18;
#X text 629 252 The coordinates for each query are updated every 100ms \, however the query is not sent until the end of each sample interval., f 28;
#X text 541 459 Query coordinates are also clipped to a set range. This range may need to be updated if you are using your own sample corpus., f 32;
#X text 586 345 The query coordinates have a starting value. The may need to be updated if you are using your own sample corpus., f 30;
#X text 184 741 The coordinates are used to find the index for that sample. This index is used to tell the sampler which buffer to access from the "clone" object., f 34;
#X text -746 65 Triggers are recieved from the sequencer to tell the voice when to play. Indexes tell the sampler which buffer to play the sample from., f 89;
