#X text 27 25 The clock sets the tempo for the whole system and splits one bar into 16 steps. The current step is communicated to the sequencer so it knows which drum voices to activate., f 45;
#X text 353 24 The sequencer receives an integer from "pd clock" telling it the current step. It then sends a trigger to corresponding voice classes., f 37;
#X text 622 26 The sampler loads all sample files into buffers on startup so that they are stored in RAM on Bela., f 26;
#X text 31 352 Programmable 16 step sequencer. Loadbangs default to a classic four-on-the-floor beat. Signals sent to "pd sequencer"., f 47;
#X text 79 515 Voice classes for kick \, hat and snare. Subpatches deal with sampling \, querying and crossfading., f 35;
#X text 30 656 Arrays for storing the current sample query, f 23;
#X text 30 734 Declaration of the Fluid Corpus Manipulation Toolbox library. Required to run the toolbox in Bela., f 36;
#X text 786 250 Reads the Text file containing sample file paths alongside their unique identifier., f 23;
#X text 401 248 Constructs a kdtree over the corpus \, allowing nearest neighbour lookup upon receival of query coordinates., f 27;
#X text 610 251 Reads the JSON file containing drum sample corpus coordinates and unique identifiers., f 23;
#X text 813 26 This version of the system uses learned mappings. Pitch/Roll/Yaw and Acceleration values are mapped to query coordinates via pathways learned by a neural network., f 42;
